  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Depth from the road",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Depth from the road\"**\n\nThe site is a nautical chart laid over land. The road network plays the coastline and distance from it plays depth: the ground is sounded in six stepped bands that deepen away from every drivable way, and each pole is written as the chart's deepest sounding. Panels are chart buff paper with black lettering; chart blue draws the controls and links; magenta, as on a real chart, marks notes, cautions and the current selection. The night scheme is a bridge display (ECDIS night palette): blue-black ground, dimmed buff lettering, a ramp that brightens with distance.\n\nOne owner amendment departs from the Admiralty palette: the depth bands are a park-map green, not chart blue, because blue on land read as water or ice. Blue therefore owns the ranking's water tint and the controls, never the land. The satellite basemap stays the default and is desaturated toward buff so the green soundings lead.\n\nDensity is a working chart's: ruled, numbered, small type, tabular figures, no decoration that does not carry a reading.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Chart grammar throughout: title block (cartouche), numbered notes, soundings, depth scale, graduated neatline, one compass rose.",
      "Upright roman capitals for names, italic for soundings and anything that reads a measurement.",
      "Square, ruled forms: 2px corners on controls, 0 on the framed sheets.",
      "Light soft shadow only where a sheet floats over the map.",
